WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:01.630
Oooohh god, okay, good morning, John.

00:00:01.630 --> 00:00:02.630
VidCon is happening.

00:00:02.630 --> 00:00:06.190
I don't know how I'm going to make my video
this week.

00:00:06.190 --> 00:00:09.710
I didn't prepare properly, so let's go do
this!

00:00:09.710 --> 00:00:12.660
I just have time to go start rehearsing with
The Perfect Strangers.

00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:14.639
And there's definitely, I don't have my hotel
key.

00:00:14.639 --> 00:00:15.639
This is hard.

00:00:15.639 --> 00:00:20.860
This is the battery for my phone, which is,
like, 4 or 5 times bigger than my phone because

00:00:20.860 --> 00:00:22.980
it needs to be charged like 3 times, I'm not
wearing shoes.

00:00:22.980 --> 00:00:23.980
That's not what elevators are supposed to
do.

00:00:23.980 --> 00:00:26.850
This is the first person to ask me for a picture.

00:00:26.850 --> 00:00:27.850
[Guy with camera] Okay.

00:00:27.850 --> 00:00:30.050
Oh I don't have my pass yet, so I can't go
in there.

00:00:30.050 --> 00:00:32.410
And I'm not even on the floor I wanna be on
yet.

00:00:32.410 --> 00:00:33.410
What's that gonna be?

00:00:33.410 --> 00:00:34.820
So I haven't gone on the escalator.

00:00:34.820 --> 00:00:38.440
I realized I didn't have my badge, so I wasn't
allowed to go to any of the places that I

00:00:38.440 --> 00:00:39.440
needed to go.

00:00:39.440 --> 00:00:40.600
...the shirts...what were they doing up there?

00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:42.100
[Dave] I couldn't get into the warehouse in
time.

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:43.200
Ohh.. *shudder sound*

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:46.930
That was Dave, our warehouse manager, and
also merch manager at VidCon.

00:00:46.930 --> 00:00:49.170
Also writer for SciShow, and also a really
good friend of mine.

00:00:49.170 --> 00:00:50.170
It's Michael Gardner.

00:00:50.170 --> 00:00:51.170
[Michael] Hey!

00:00:51.170 --> 00:00:52.170
Woo!

00:00:52.170 --> 00:00:53.170
Who, how's, how you feelin'?

00:00:53.170 --> 00:00:54.170
[Michael] Great!

00:00:54.170 --> 00:00:55.170
This is Julie, sometimes I tweet about Julie.

00:00:55.170 --> 00:00:56.170
[Julie] Hi!

00:00:56.170 --> 00:00:57.170
This is who Julie is, she makes my life work.

00:00:57.170 --> 00:00:58.170
[Julie] Most of the time.

00:00:58.170 --> 00:00:59.289
The expo hall getting set up.

00:00:59.289 --> 00:01:01.250
All the escalators are off.

00:01:01.250 --> 00:01:02.460
This...this is Rob!

00:01:02.460 --> 00:01:04.719
Waiting for me, outside the room.

00:01:04.719 --> 00:01:06.149
[Rob] Hey!

00:01:06.149 --> 00:01:07.579
*rehearsal music*

00:01:07.579 --> 00:01:12.450
Rehearsal had to take a break for bean bag
mountain.

00:01:12.450 --> 00:01:18.020
*rehearsal music*

00:01:18.020 --> 00:01:21.359
Bury me in bean bags!

00:01:21.359 --> 00:01:25.170
I don't wanna know about the world anymore!

00:01:25.170 --> 00:01:26.639
It's too hard!

00:01:26.639 --> 00:01:29.969
I'm like four bean bags down now.

00:01:29.969 --> 00:01:32.249
Leaving rehearsal, Craig needs me.

00:01:32.249 --> 00:01:33.249
Craig WheezyWaiter.

00:01:33.249 --> 00:01:36.959
I don't know why he needs me for, what for,
but he does, so I'm gonna go find him.

00:01:36.959 --> 00:01:40.219
[WheezyWaiter] I run off stage, I run out
of the convention center, and I'm in the desert,

00:01:40.219 --> 00:01:42.844
running into the desert, which I already have
footage of.

00:01:42.844 --> 00:01:43.844
I found John!

00:01:43.844 --> 00:01:44.844
[John] Helloo!

00:01:44.844 --> 00:01:47.069
Just by the way, my badge has higher clearance
than John's.

00:01:47.069 --> 00:01:48.600
[John] To me, that represents progress.

00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:52.549
Okay this is kind of moment of truth for me,
I haven't seen the stage or the arena yet

00:01:52.549 --> 00:01:53.549
at all.

00:01:53.549 --> 00:01:54.549
Wooaaahhh.

00:01:54.549 --> 00:01:57.189
Okay, that's pretty cool.

00:01:57.189 --> 00:02:01.009
I'm very thirsty but it's very difficult for
me to drink these drinks because I know how

00:02:01.009 --> 00:02:02.299
much they cost, but I'm doing it anyway.

00:02:02.299 --> 00:02:03.759
Our pillows are, apparently, semi-sentient.

00:02:03.759 --> 00:02:05.421
This is what it looks like backstage at VidCon.

00:02:05.421 --> 00:02:07.340
This is what my dad looks like.

00:02:07.340 --> 00:02:08.340
Oh, things!

00:02:08.340 --> 00:02:09.340
All the wires!

00:02:09.340 --> 00:02:10.340
Is that Tyler?

00:02:10.340 --> 00:02:12.730
[Tyler] It's Tyler Oakley!

00:02:12.730 --> 00:02:14.770
Hi Tyler!

00:02:14.770 --> 00:02:16.810
Hi, Troye!

00:02:16.810 --> 00:02:21.489
This is the part where we talk about how we're
going to do what we're gonna do, figure out

00:02:21.489 --> 00:02:26.120
what kind of mics we need, uh, Monica tells
us what to do, basically.

00:02:26.120 --> 00:02:28.160
We rehearsed, and now John is off to do an
Ear Biscuit.

00:02:28.160 --> 00:02:30.739
I need a moral of the story, what's the moral
of the story?

00:02:30.739 --> 00:02:37.530
[John] The moral of the story is that your
ability to come up with new ideas and execute

00:02:37.530 --> 00:02:39.489
them continues to astonish me.

00:02:39.489 --> 00:02:40.489
Aww...

00:02:40.489 --> 00:02:44.000
[John] but not in a good way really, more
in an overwhelmed way, so don't say awww.

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:46.500
Just checking out what's going on in the expo
hall now.

00:02:46.500 --> 00:02:50.269
I just got a Ze hug.

00:02:50.269 --> 00:02:52.540
Everything we're touring with fits in one
elevator.

00:02:52.540 --> 00:02:55.640
This guy grabbed the drum that fell off the
cart.

00:02:55.640 --> 00:02:56.640
Thank you.

00:02:56.640 --> 00:02:58.870
Now I'm back in my hotel room, because I had
to grab my computer so that I can go do a

00:02:58.870 --> 00:03:02.249
technical rehearsal, which is where your computer
into a thing and you see if your PowerPoint

00:03:02.249 --> 00:03:03.249
presentation is going to work.

00:03:03.249 --> 00:03:05.689
I think VidCon is mostly walking, for me.

00:03:05.689 --> 00:03:06.769
This is a big room.

00:03:06.769 --> 00:03:09.280
This is where I'm giving my Industry presentation.

00:03:09.280 --> 00:03:15.049
Now I'm at a welcome party welcoming people
who came to help us out at VidCon.

00:03:15.049 --> 00:03:16.049
Ahhhhh!

00:03:16.049 --> 00:03:17.049
Sorry.

00:03:17.049 --> 00:03:18.049
Just being excited.

00:03:18.049 --> 00:03:19.049
Hey, everybody, it's Natalie Tran!

00:03:19.049 --> 00:03:20.079
[Natalie] Oh are you filming?

00:03:20.079 --> 00:03:21.079
Oh!

00:03:21.079 --> 00:03:25.560
The first thing when you meet a new YouTuber
is you're like "You're not average height."

00:03:25.560 --> 00:03:27.659
So I was like, you're super short and she
was like you're super tall.

00:03:27.659 --> 00:03:30.010
[Natalie] You're so short yourself.

00:03:30.010 --> 00:03:31.829
Yay, hey, Katherine's here.

00:03:31.829 --> 00:03:33.190
[Katherine] (sigh) Yeah!

00:03:33.190 --> 00:03:34.540
You made it!

00:03:34.540 --> 00:03:38.939
Freaking Natalie Tran gave me TimTams; this
is the best thing.

00:03:38.939 --> 00:03:40.120
Aheheheh...

00:03:40.120 --> 00:03:42.140
That was the day before VidCon started.

00:03:42.140 --> 00:03:44.319
John, I'll see you in the morning.

